v 3
d whodropped: which variables cost you observations?
d
d whodropped reports, for each variable in a specification, how many
d observations it is missing for, how many observations it alone is
d responsible for losing, and the marginal cost of imposing it. Run
d after an estimation command it also reconciles the complete-case
d count against e(sample), so that losses which are not due to missing
d values appear as a separate residual.
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260828
d
d Author: Ali C. Akyol, Telfer School of Management, University of Ottawa
d Support: email aliakyol@outlook.com
d
f whodropped.ado
f whodropped.sthlp
